* JUSTIFICATION: Unknown, seems high compared to constrained average

*~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* radius_cp_coolant_channel = 3.0E-3 
* DESCRIPTION:   Average Radius of Coolant Channel for CP (m) 
* JUSTIFICATION: Assumed

* temp_cp_coolant_inlet = 20.0 
* DESCRIPTION:   Centrepost Coolant Inlet Temperature (K) 
* JUSTIFICATION: Choosen to be optimal after a scan ranging from 15 to 30 K (G. Voss and S. Kahn)

*~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* icc = 43
* DESCRIPTION:   Average Centrepost Temperature Consistency (TART)
* JUSTIFICATION: Consistency equation, not turned on
* VARIABLES:     itart.  tcpav2 calculated in-situ

*ixc = 20
*temp_cp_average = 20.42
*boundl(20) = 20.0
*boundu(20) = 25.0
* DESCRIPTION:   Average temperature of centrepost
* JUSTIFICATION: 

*~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

*icc = 53
* DESCRIPTION:   Constraint equation for fast neutron fluence on TF coil upper limit
* JUSTIFICATION: Turned off, do not care about TF coil fluence.
* VARIABLES:     flu_tf_neutron_fast_max(max fast neutron fluence on TF coil (n/m2)),flu_tf_neutron_fast_peak calculated in situ

* flu_tf_neutron_fast_max = 
* DESCRIPTION:   max fast neutron fluence on TF coil (n/m2) (`blktmodel>0`) (`constraint equation 53`)
* Also used for demountable magnets (itart = 1) and superconducting coils (i_tf_sup = 1)
* To set the CP lifetime (`constraint equation 85`) 
* JUSTIFICATION: Not set, not using icc = 53

